# GEODROP — INSTALLED-BASE NICHE OWNERSHIP ENGINE

## MISSION

Discover and fully justify country-specific ecommerce niches where we can plausibly become the canonical compatibility and purchase layer rather than merely another seller.

Do not search for “winning products.”

Search for neglected INSTALLED BASES.

The atomic opportunity is:

COUNTRY
× INSTALLED ASSET
× GENERATION / REVISION
× LIFECYCLE TRIGGER
× COMPONENT
× COMPATIBILITY UNCERTAINTY
× LOCAL SUPPLIER GRAPH

The target pattern is:

1. A durable asset/system was installed in meaningful numbers over many years.
2. The installed asset remains in use much longer than individual components, consumables or technologies.
3. Owners eventually need a filter, hose, control, sensor, motor, cartridge, valve, board, adapter, receiver, accessory, successor unit, upgrade or other specific component.
4. Determining the correct component requires model/generation/revision/interface/supersession knowledge.
5. The wrong part creates meaningful friction, delay, return cost or equipment downtime.
6. Good local physical supply exists.
7. Existing suppliers are operationally competent but their consumer-facing data is fragmented, trade-oriented, PDF-bound, poorly localized, inconsistent or difficult for agents to reason over.
8. No excellent local merchant currently owns the end-to-end identity → compatibility → exclusion → supersession → availability → checkout decision.
9. We can model the important decision surface with a relatively bounded catalog rather than an enormous undifferentiated marketplace.
10. We can compile the resulting graph into Google Merchant Center, Shopify Catalog, native-language web pages and agent-readable endpoints.

The company being built is a COMPATIBILITY COMMERCE COMPILER.

Each accepted niche is a bounded country/product subgraph generated from one canonical backend.

