## STRICT EPISTEMIC RULES

Use live web research.

Research in the native language of every target country as well as English.

Prefer primary sources:

1. OEM manuals, catalogs, old manuals, service documentation and replacement guides.
2. Manufacturer product pages and archived model documentation.
3. Official distributors and wholesalers.
4. Current retailers and comparison engines.
5. Government/trade/industry installed-base statistics.
6. Repair/service specialists.
7. Trade forums and technical communities.
8. Reddit and homeowner/operator communities for first-hand friction.
9. Search result composition and marketplaces.
10. High-quality secondary research only when primary evidence is unavailable.

Every material fact must have:

* source URL;
* observation date;
* source type;
* evidence grade;
* exact model/country context;
* independence cluster.

UNKNOWN beats assumption.

Never invent:

* installed base;
* search volume;
* CPC;
* conversion rate;
* supplier cost;
* margin;
* reseller status;
* stock;
* failure rate;
* replacement interval;
* return rate.

Do not treat five retailers using the same distributor feed as five independent supply sources.

