## PHASE 2 — INSTALLED-BASE PROOF

Establish whether a meaningful cohort actually exists.

Seek:

* OEM disclosed unit counts;
* annual/historical sales;
* housing/building installation statistics;
* trade association statistics;
* government registers;
* historical catalogs;
* service network size;
* replacement guides referring to tens/hundreds of thousands of units;
* discontinued model archives;
* reseller/service evidence.

Record:

* estimated installed base;
* source;
* relevant generation;
* installation years;
* uncertainty;
* expected surviving cohort only if defensibly estimable.

Never infer current surviving units merely from historic sales without an explicit survival model.

A large installed base alone is insufficient.

