## PHASE 3 — LIFECYCLE TRIGGER PROOF

Determine WHY someone buys.

Map:

installed asset
→ component/problem
→ failure/replenishment/upgrade trigger
→ purchase decision.

Classify trigger:

CONSUMABLE
WEAR_PART
FAILURE
OBSOLESCENCE
SUCCESSOR_MIGRATION
COMPATIBILITY_UPGRADE
REGULATORY_REPLACEMENT
ACCESSORY_EXPANSION
DAMAGE
OTHER.

Find evidence for frequency or urgency.

Distinguish:

* routine low-value commodity maintenance;
* uncertain compatibility replacement;
* forced/urgent replacement;
* high-value successor migration.

Never assume a replacement interval across models.

