## RUN-LEVEL DISCOVERY OUTPUT

Do not pad the report.

A high-quality run should:

* mass-screen a broad set of installed-base × country cells;
* surface approximately 10–20 genuinely interesting anomalies when evidence permits;
* adversarially investigate the strongest;
* deeply construct only the few that clear structural gates;
* kill aggressively;
* fully package only those that could plausibly be owned.

Prefer:

100 cells scanned
→ 15 anomalies
→ 6 deep audits
→ 2 exceptional campaigns

over:

20 generic “product ideas.”

At the end output:

BEST NEW OWNABLE NICHE
BEST NEAR-MISS
MOST IMPORTANT KILL
NEW REUSABLE MARKET MECHANISM
HIGHEST-EVI NEXT RESEARCH ACTION.

The objective is not to discover products.

The objective is to continuously discover **small commercial knowledge graphs that nobody has bothered to own yet — and then own them completely.**
